    <completion-note>
      SERVER (ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs): the four structural ops implemented + SEQUENCED LAST (two-pass
      applier — text/mark ops first, structural collected + applied after, so text-op run-local anchors are
      unaffected; proven by Apply_StructuralOpsSequencedLast_TextAnchorUnaffected). Tracked representation is a
      paragraph-MARK revision in w:pPr/w:rPr (MarkParagraphMark): split = inserted mark on the leading para +
      trailing runs moved to a new w14:paraId (cloned pPr); merge = w:del on the TARGET (predecessor) para-mark
      glyph — bridge-prior-art #6, the hardest edge; insert = new empty para w/ inserted mark; delete = strike
      runs (w:del/w:delText) + deleted para-mark (the retired {paraId,text:''} sentinel semantic — closes task
      023 server-side). Unrepresentable edges REFUSED via new ComposePatchErrorKind.StructuralOperationRefused
      (merge across a table/section boundary, colliding newParaId, split of a field-bearing para) — handled, not
      corrupted. setBlockAttr remains at its own StructuralOpNotYetImplemented seam (outside the four-op scope).
      CLIENT (stepOperationInterceptor.ts): classifyStructuralStep diffs paraId-bearing blocks before/after a
      block-boundary ReplaceStep/ReplaceAroundStep to EMIT mergeParagraph/deleteParagraph/splitParagraph/
      insertParagraph into the RebasedOperationLog (buildAnchor + deriveOperation extended for the four types);
      whole-paragraph delete/merge is now CAPTURED, not silently deferred — closes the task-023 coverage gap
      client-side. Verify: server dotnet build clean; 547 Compose tests green (7 new structural + ordering +
      table-refusal); client typecheck clean on the two touched files (pre-existing unrelated @spaarke/ai-widgets
      module errors remain); 31 stepOperationInterceptor jest tests green (4 new structural). Publish 49.90 MB
      compressed incl PDBs (+0.27 vs ~49.63 baseline, ≤60). No NEW package / no NEW HIGH CVE (the
      System.Security.Cryptography.Xml HIGH is pre-existing transitive). ADR-007/010/013 clean; Tier-1
      NetArchTest ADR-013 green (the 3 ArchTest failures — ADR-007 Graph isolation, ADR-010 concrete/Options —
      are pre-existing whole-assembly scans, not introduced here). Do NOT commit; TASK-INDEX/current-task
      untouched per orchestrator instruction. Task 023 may now proceed (its dep on 031 is satisfied).
    </completion-note>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Extend the Patch Engine (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs`,
    built in task 030) to apply the four STRUCTURAL operations — `splitParagraph`, `mergeParagraph`,
    `insertParagraph`, `deleteParagraph` — as operations. These MUST be SEQUENCED LAST in the applier
    (after all text/mark operations) so that text-op run-local-offset anchors resolved earlier in the
    pass are not shifted by structural changes. The hardest edge is `mergeParagraph`: deleting a
    paragraph mark is a `w:del` on the para-mark glyph carried in `w:pPr/w:rPr` (bridge-prior-art
    finding #6 — the hardest OOXML edge). Continue to mutate the OpenXml DOM, never string-edit
    `document.xml`. This is a MODIFY of task 030's engine, not a new file. Keep the engine stateless,
    `byte[]`-in/`byte[]`-out, no AI internals.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 / Open XML SDK developer who understands OOXML paragraph structure (`w:p`, `w:pPr`,
    `w:rPr` para-mark, section breaks, tables) and the tracked-change representation of structural edits
    (a merged paragraph = a tracked deletion of the paragraph mark, not a naive node removal).
  </role>

  <goal>
    The Patch Engine applies split/merge/insert/delete paragraph as first-class operations, sequenced
    last so text-op anchors are unaffected, with paragraph-mark deletion (merge) represented as a
    `w:del` on the para-mark glyph in `w:pPr/w:rPr`; each structural op round-trips correctly on the
    corpus, and an edge that cannot be represented safely (e.g. merging a paragraph into a following
    table) is refused rather than corrupting the package.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 (structural ops applied natively — the capability the paragraph-diff never had), §5.6
      pitfall (b) "paragraph-mark deletion = `w:del` on the para-mark glyph in `w:pPr/w:rPr` — the
      hardest edge". Spec FR-05 acceptance: each structural op round-trips (incl. paragraph-mark
      deletion via `w:pPr/w:rPr/w:del`). Owner clarification: structural edits are IN core, sequenced
      last. Task 030 built the text/mark applier + resolve-by-paraId; this task adds the structural
      layer on top and enforces its ordering-last discipline.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs — add splitParagraph / mergeParagraph / insertParagraph / deleteParagraph applied LAST in the operation pass; merge = `w:del` on the para-mark in `w:pPr/w:rPr`</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ — task 003 operation-schema structural op types (`splitParagraph`/`mergeParagraph`/`insertParagraph`/`deleteParagraph`/`setBlockAttr`)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5 (Patch backend, structural ops), §5.6 pitfall (b)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-05</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">`ComposeShadowPatchEngine` core (text/mark applier + resolve-by-paraId + native w:ins/w:del/w:comment) — this task extends it with structural ops.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-05">The engine MUST support paragraph split / merge / insert / delete as operations; each MUST round-trip correctly on the corpus, including paragraph-mark deletion via `w:pPr/w:rPr/w:del`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / ordering">Structural ops MUST be SEQUENCED LAST in the applier (after all text/mark ops) so text-op run-local-offset anchors resolved earlier are not shifted by structural changes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / NFR-01">Mutate the OpenXml DOM, NEVER string-edit `document.xml`; untouched subtrees stay byte-identical.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007 / ADR-010 / ADR-013">Engine stays `byte[]`-in/`byte[]`-out, stateless concrete singleton, no AI internals (Tier-1 NetArchTest green) — unchanged from task 030.</constraint>
