      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/bridge-prior-art.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Paragraph-mark deletion (merge)" location="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/bridge-prior-art.md finding #6 / design §5.6(b)">
        Merging two paragraphs = a tracked deletion of the first paragraph's mark: `w:del` on the para-mark glyph carried in `w:pPr/w:rPr`, NOT a naive removal of the `w:p` node. The hardest structural edge — model it explicitly.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Sequence-structural-last" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs">
        Apply all text/mark ops (offset-anchored) first, then apply structural ops, so structural node changes never invalidate an earlier text-op's run-local-offset anchor.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration. Confirm task 030 is complete (the engine exists). Read the task 003 structural op-type definitions. Load knowledge files + `bff-extensions.md`; state the Placement Justification for the PR.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Insert / delete / split paragraph">Implement `insertParagraph` (new `w:p` at the anchor, carrying a fresh `w14:paraId`), `deleteParagraph` (tracked deletion of the `w:p`), and `splitParagraph` (divide a `w:p` at the run-local-offset, preserving `w:pPr` on the resulting paragraphs). Mutate the DOM.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Merge paragraph — the hardest edge">Implement `mergeParagraph` as a `w:del` on the para-mark glyph in the first paragraph's `w:pPr/w:rPr` (bridge-prior-art (b)), joining the runs. Handle the boundary case where the following block is a table or a section break — refuse/guard rather than corrupt.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Sequence structural ops last">Ensure the applier applies structural ops AFTER all text/mark ops in the pass, so earlier text-op run-local-offset anchors are unaffected. Add focused unit tests for ordering under `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/`.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Build + verify">Build the BFF; run the Tier-1 NetArchTest facade check; run existing `Services/Compose` unit tests (no regression). Round-trip proof lands in the task 034 seam slices.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Size/CVE + index + deviations">Publish; report absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB (≤60 MB); `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` (no new HIGH CVE). Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs (extended — split/merge/insert/delete paragraph, sequenced last; merge via w:pPr/w:rPr/w:del)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ (structural-op unit tests, incl. ordering + para-mark deletion)</output>
